# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-8, 2.1-21, C-10, RC-9). L §5.7 Parts and lifespans: "a party's parts must be gone by the
# end of its lifespan. That is checked after the whole order of the lifespan's last day"; E §4.2 step 5: "a party whose
# lifespan ends on t and that holds a part at the close of t refuses that part's place from t on (RUN-LIFESPAN)"; L §8.4
# `<party> ends on <d> holding parts of <place>`. tomek lives to 2026-04-01 and holds t1's 50.00 then.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if w in withdrawals and k.owner == w.paid_from then 0 else 1
kind withdrawals: transfers
  attr paid_from: key persons
kind tomeks: transfers
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1_day: date
input a1_amt: money PLN
input t1_day: date
input t1_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
  rule t beats base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in tomeks
move a1: transfers
  on a1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1_amt
move t1: tomeks
  on t1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount t1_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-04-01), bal(konto, 2026-04-30) of ania

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..2026-04-01
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  a1_day = 2026-02-01
  a1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  t1_day = 2026-02-02
  t1_amt = 50.00 PLN
=== expect
q: (150.00 PLN, refused: RUN-LIFESPAN tomek ends on 2026-04-01 holding parts of konto, refused: RUN-LIFESPAN tomek ends on 2026-04-01 holding parts of konto)
  cut 2026-01-01
